    <item>
      <title>TotK - Legacy Dungeon Items - complete version.</title>
      <author>Porroman420</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/693923</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/693923#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">2ddb20fc9f006170fbf10ccfb2d5ea89a444ae55</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:24:20 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d6dd2d712.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d4d4b7c66.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d591e75a8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d93a63b1e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d964ccd27.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d969d360d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d96cc82c1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d97889a63.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a54d9927fd3e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Ghost fuses options&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now the tkcl file has options to make your items don't have ghost fuses :&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The MasterSword subtype enables the ghost fuses, but also will cause odd behavior like making weapons say "the master sword broke" or make them unable to be displayed at Link's house.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Now the tkcl has options to choose if you want the ghost fuses or not.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Ghost fuses  =  the weapons will say "the master sword broke" despite them not being one, weapons can't be displayed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Withouth Ghost fuses = the weapon will behave as the rest, you will be able to display them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;No other changes were made, update if you want to get rid of the ghost fuses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want this set of options delete your previous install and use this one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Adjustment&lt;/em&gt;: Added tkcl options for ghost fuse&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;A mysterious figure is waiting for you at the top of the Temple of Time in the sky...waiting to offer you a reward.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is the full complete version of Tears of the Kingdom - Legacy dungeon items, which brings some items from past entries as new dungeon treasures for this game, packed alongside a small quest so you can get and know all the items, the custom special guest also works as a shop that sells useful disposable materials.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This version changes small things from the standalone versions while fixing some bugs from the cane of somaria standalone version too, each dungeon item comes from a different Zelda game, i decided to make the ones that are weapons breakable, but all have 800 durability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;-The Legend of Zelda - Wind Waker :&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Wind Waker, found at the Wind temple can create an updraft when you swing it without a fuse, when fused will shoot elemental "wind" depending on the element the fuse you decide to use with, can reutilize one hit fuses like the Forest Dweller Sword, shockproof and fireproof.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;-The Legend of Zelda - Ocarina of Time:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Goron's Bracelet found inside the Fire temple deals physical + fire damage, it's goron fire projectiles can destroy any kind of breakable rock (rock walls, ore deposits, marbled rock legs), can warm link up on ice enviroments, and acts as a light source in the depths too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;-The Legend of Zelda - A Link to the past:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Cane of Somaria found inside the Thunder Temple when unfused will cast a blinding light spark that can trigger light switches, as those found inside the Thunder Dungeon, when fused with any monster part that gives elemental fire attacks will summon on swing explosive cubes with a custom animation as they are similar to a zonai timerbomb, you can pick them up, fuse them to your weapons or your shields (all previous bugs fixed), the cane has a limit of 8 cubes, once you summon all 8 you must change weapons to restore it's energy (swapping weapons with the dpad also works)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;- The Legend of Zelda - Twilight Princess:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Horsecall Whistle\Ilia's Charm also on the whereabouts of the Water temple, this will let you summon your horse on places they can naturally be, if you happen to summon your horse on a "forbidden place" you can re-summon him twice on places they can be to make it re-appear.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;AND THE LAST DUNGEON ITEM :  The Legend of Zelda - Phantom Hourglass:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Phantom Hourglass can be found just behind the locked door after starting Mineru's part of the game, at your disposal &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;this item will prevent all gloom damage by contact for 10 minutes, the counter stops if you are not in contact with ANY source of gloom, also it can automatically revert up to 10 times any ammount of broken hearts gloom enemies may do to you&lt;/span&gt;, (for example, if an enemy does 1 broken heart damage your hearts are not gonna decrease beyond, unless it does a stronger attack that deals more, in any case any X ammount of this type of damage will be reverted to empty hearts)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;ALSO the effect works over armors that give gloom protective extra hearts and yellow hearts, these will be protected, i recommend you to let your armors that give such fully recharge before stepping into goo :D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;once the 10:00 timer stops the hourglass will enter into a cooldown of the same amount of time, this will also happen if the hourglass reverts damage ten times, hourglass lifepoints and gloom contact timer are separate, so you can save your last minute for combat or your last hitpoint for exploring (or escaping from Gloom hands haha)...&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;once the hourglass enters to sleep you will get one full life heal + extra life + no broken hearts (will not prevent one shot death tho)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/totk_-_new_dungeon_items_c37c6.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/totk_-_legacy_dungeon_items.zip" type="application/zip"/>
