    <item>
      <title>Draconic Gale: Speed Unbound</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/707603</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/707603#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a4b770de5f70ebd8528f123d7e6d9b08dcb7f3bd</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:15:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a8867313a5e1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a886721f09ac.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a886b6c96d4d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a886710b45dd.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Draconic Gale: Speed Unbound&lt;/h1&gt;&#13;
&lt;i&gt;Unleash the true fury of Hyrule's ancient sky gods&lt;/i&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Tired of watching the Dragons lazily drift across the sky while you wait for that one horn shard to drop?&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This mod lets you &lt;b&gt;independently control the flight speed&lt;/b&gt; of every permanent Dragon in Tears of the Kingdom.&#13;
No more slow, peaceful sky snakes - these are &lt;i&gt;ancient elemental gods&lt;/i&gt;, and now they fly like it.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT THIS MOD DOES&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each Dragon gets its own &lt;b&gt;option group&lt;/b&gt; in TKMM, so you can mix and match speeds freely:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Farosh - The Stormbound Dragon&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;i&gt;Faron · Lake Hylia · Gerudo Highlands · Depths&lt;/i&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The lightning Long that erupts from Lake Floria at dawn.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose: &lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Naydra - The Ice Dragon&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;i&gt;Lanayru · Necluda · Depths&lt;/i&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The frost Wyrm that descends from Mount Lanayru under frozen skies.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose: &lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dinraal - The Fire Dragon&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;i&gt;Eldin · Akkala · Deep Akkala · Depths&lt;/i&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The infernal Drake that patrols the volcanic skies above Death Mountain.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose: &lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Light Dragon - The Sacred Long&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;i&gt;Roams all of Hyrule at extreme altitude&lt;/i&gt;&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The sacred Dragon born from a princess's sacrifice.&#13;
Both phases are affected - the high-altitude wanderer &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; the spiraling descent.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose: &lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;SPEED REFERENCE&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; - Original speed (~80 u/s). No modifications applied.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; - 160 u/s. Noticeably faster, still cinematic.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; - 400 u/s. Dragons blaze across the sky. Good for farming.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt; - 800 u/s. &lt;i&gt;Absolute madness.&lt;/i&gt; Blink and they're gone.&#13;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;u/s = internal game units per second. Vanilla rail speed is approximately 80 u/s.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;HOW IT WORKS - DUAL-LAYER PATCHING&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod patches &lt;b&gt;two parameter layers simultaneously&lt;/b&gt; without conflicting with $parent settings.&#13;
The game's Dragons use a deep inheritance chain with multiple fallback levels - a naive single-layer patch only works for the first few seconds before the runtime overwrites it.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Layer 1 - Global Scene Parameters&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;Scene/Component/DragonMgrParam/Default.game__scene__DragonMgrParam.bgyml&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
Injects &lt;b&gt;DesiredLinearSpeed&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;MaxAcceleration&lt;/b&gt; into each Dragon's&#13;
&lt;b&gt;DragonInfoList[N].RailMoveSetting.MoveParam&lt;/b&gt;.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Layer 2 - Actor Parameters (No $parent conflicts)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;Pack/Actor/Enemy_Dragon_*.pack.zs&#13;
  → Component/DragonParam/*.bgyml&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
Modifies &lt;b&gt;MoveParamVariation.Basic&lt;/b&gt; for initial state.&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Replaces the &lt;b&gt;$parent&lt;/b&gt; reference in &lt;b&gt;RailMoveSetting&lt;/b&gt; with fully explicit values to prevent rail-transition engine crashes while guaranteeing speed changes remain permanent throughout the entire flight route.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;INSTALLATION&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Method A - Using TKMM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Download and install &lt;b&gt;TKMM&lt;/b&gt; (TotK Mod Manager) if you haven't already&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Download &lt;b&gt;Faster_Dragons.tkcl&lt;/b&gt; from this page&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Drag and drop the &lt;b&gt;.tkcl&lt;/b&gt; file into the TKMM window&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The mod will appear with &lt;b&gt;4 option groups&lt;/b&gt; - one for each Dragon&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Select your desired speed for each Dragon independently:&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Vanilla&lt;/b&gt; - Original speed, no changes&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;2× Swiftness&lt;/b&gt; - 160 u/s. Noticeably faster, still cinematic&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;5× Speed&lt;/b&gt; - 400 u/s. Dragons blaze across the sky&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;10× Power&lt;/b&gt; - 800 u/s. Blink and the Dragon is gone&#13;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol start="6"&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;b&gt;Apply&lt;/b&gt; and launch the game&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;Each Dragon's speed is independent - you can set Naydra to 10× while keeping Farosh at 2×.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Method B - Building from Source&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
If you want to customize the speed values or rebuild the mod yourself:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Requirements:&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;Python 3.8+&#13;
pip install oead byml zstandard&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Steps:&lt;/b&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Download &lt;b&gt;build_faster_dragons.py&lt;/b&gt; from this page&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Open it in a text editor and set the paths at the top:&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;# Root of your dumped TotK romfs&#13;
ROMFS_DIR = Path("~/TOTK/1").expanduser()&#13;
&#13;
# Zstandard dictionary for .pack.zs files&#13;
PACK_DICT = Path("~/TOTK/pack.zsdic").expanduser()&#13;
&#13;
# Output directory&#13;
OUT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "faster_Dragons"&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Optionally edit the &lt;b&gt;SPEEDS&lt;/b&gt; list to add custom speed tiers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Run: &lt;pre&gt;python3 build_faster_Dragons.py&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The output &lt;b&gt;Faster_Dragons.tkcl&lt;/b&gt; will be in the &lt;b&gt;faster_dragons/&lt;/b&gt; folder&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Import it into TKMM as described in Method A&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;FAQ&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does this work with other Dragon mods?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Yes.&lt;/b&gt; This mod uses TKMM's TYPE_CHANGELOG (3-way BYML merge), so it's compatible&#13;
with texture swaps, model replacements, and other Dragon mods.&#13;
The only potential conflict is with mods that also modify DragonParam speed values.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does this affect cutscenes?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;No.&lt;/b&gt; Cutscene Dragons use separate animation sequences that are not affected&#13;
by the rail movement parameters this mod changes.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Can I change speed mid-playthrough?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Yes.&lt;/b&gt; Just change the options in TKMM, re-apply, and restart the game.&#13;
No save corruption - the mod only changes parameter files, not save data.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;fieldset&gt;&#13;
&lt;legend&gt;&lt;b&gt;Which game version is supported?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/legend&gt;&#13;
Built and tested against &lt;b&gt;TotK v1.2.0&lt;/b&gt;.&#13;
Uses &lt;b&gt;TKMM format v32&lt;/b&gt;.&#13;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;COMPATIBILITY&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;TotK v1.2.0&lt;/b&gt; - built and tested against this version&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;TKMM format v32&lt;/b&gt; - uses TYPE_CHANGELOG (3-way merge), not full file replacement&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Safe to combine&lt;/b&gt; with other Dragon mods (texture swaps, model replacements, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
